Source: https://github.com/YadeWira/omega-srep, branch osrep, tag orep-v0.0.6
        (commit b9125f1126bdc2b14dcc290a666f8bb5af67c66d), release asset orep-unit-0.0.6.tar.gz
        (sha256 in the release's SHA256SUMS).

Files copied unchanged from orep-unit-0.0.6.tar.gz:
  orep.pas         the Pascal unit (API, framing, decoder, Pascal reference of the core)
  orep_core.c      the native match finder and CRC-32C (freestanding C, no libc)
  orep-format.md   the stream format
  orep.md          the unit's documentation (Spanish)
  LICENSE          MIT

The prebuilt objects of the tarball (obj/<target>/orep_core.o) are not vendored: build.sh
compiles orep_core.c for every target with the compiler of that target and the flags of the
tarball's README (-O2 -fno-builtin -ffreestanding -fno-stack-protector
-fno-tree-loop-distribute-patterns). -dOREP_NO_NATIVE uses the Pascal reference instead (same
bytes; tests/orep.sh checks it). Do not edit these files: update them from a new OREP release.
